<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
Ukrainian translation — full UI coverage. Formal ви-form throughout
(consistent with the existing strings' imperative style: "Натисніть",
"Одягніть", "Візьміть").

What is NOT overridden, by design:
- `app_name` — brand identifier, identical across locales.
- `insight_time_am` / `_pm` / `_midnight` / `_noon` (and *_minutes
  variants) — English-only spoken-time formatter helpers. Ukrainian
  uses `insight_time_hour` / `_hour_minutes` ("15" / "15:30") which
  are translated below; the AM/PM keys exist for the
  `Locale.language == "en"` path only and would never be read in a uk
  runtime.

Quotes around nested labels use Ukrainian guillemet «…» — locale-native
style. Brand "ClothesCast" stays in Latin script.

Picker labels under `settings_region_language_*` and
`settings_tts_voice_locale_*` give the Ukrainian names for every offered
locale (Англійська (США), Французька (Канада), Китайська (спрощена), …).
The locale tag stored on disk (en-US / fr-CA / zh-CN) is unchanged;
only the displayed label localizes.
-->
